-- Purely administrative machinery with no fact any rule in this Part (or
-- elsewhere in the corpus) would test is recorded as inert prose rather than
-- force-fit into a meaningless predicate: ss. 9(2), 9A(5), 10AA(5), 10AB(1),
-- 11(1)-(2), 11A, 13A(1) and (3)-(6), 13B(2). Each is noted plainly at its
-- site below, following the s. 33D(3) saving-clause precedent in
-- dog-act-1976.l4.
--
-- Numbering note: ss. 10, 10AA, 10AB, 10A appear in exactly that order in the
-- source compilation -- 10AA and 10AB were inserted (2013) before 10A's own
-- insertion point in the section sequence, so "10A" sorts after "10AB" in the
-- Act's own numbering. Preserved here, not corrected.
--
-- No regulative (PARTY/MUST/WITHIN) rules appear in this file: none of the
-- assigned sections state a numeric deadline ("within N days" or similar) --
-- the duties here are either open-ended ("must appoint", "must establish and
-- maintain"), triggered by an unscheduled event ("at the reasonable request
-- of"), or periodic without a fixed-length window ("at least once every
-- financial year", modelled below as a day/year-count predicate instead).
