§ `Part II -- Administration`
§§ `9. Administrative responsibility`

-- s. 9(1): the duty to administer and enforce the Act is not itself a fact
-- another rule would test. The one operative fact in this subsection is the
-- Governor's power, by Order, to deem an outside area to be within a local
-- government's district; that deeming is what downstream jurisdictional
-- questions (e.g. s. 10(2) below) would care about.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9(1)
GIVEN `a s 9(1) Order has been made declaring the area to be within the district for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the area is treated as within the local government's district under s 9(1)` `a s 9(1) Order has been made declaring the area to be within the district for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
    `a s 9(1) Order has been made declaring the area to be within the district for the purposes of this Act`

-- s. 9(2): a savings clause -- nothing in s. 9(1) prevents the CEO from
-- performing the CEO's functions, or from doing anything the CEO considers
-- appropriate for performing them. No fact this Part's rules would test;
-- recorded here as inert prose, per the s. 33D(3) precedent.

§§ `9A. Delegation by CEO`

DECLARE `S9A Delegation` HAS
    `in writing`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the CEO`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9A(1)-(2)
GIVEN d IS A `S9A Delegation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 9A delegation is validly made` d MEANS
    d's `in writing` AND d's `signed by the CEO`

-- s. 9A(3): a person to whom a power or duty is delegated under this section
-- cannot delegate it onward -- an absolute bar, not conditioned on any fact.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9A(3)
`a s 9A delegate may validly sub-delegate the power or duty` MEANS FALSE

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9A(4)
GIVEN `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the CEO's delegate is presumed to have acted within the terms of the s 9A delegation` `the contrary is shown` MEANS
    NOT `the contrary is shown`

-- s. 9A(5): the section does not limit the CEO's ability to perform a
-- function through an officer or agent. No fact this Part's rules would
-- test; recorded here as inert prose.

§§ `9B. Designated persons`

DECLARE `S9B Authorisation` HAS
    `made in writing by the CEO`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `cancelled by the CEO`         IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9B(1)
GIVEN a IS A `S9B Authorisation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 9B(1) authorisation is validly made` a MEANS
    a's `made in writing by the CEO`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9B(2)(b)
GIVEN a IS A `S9B Authorisation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 9B authorisation remains in force` a MEANS
    a's `made in writing by the CEO` AND NOT a's `cancelled by the CEO`

-- s. 9B(2)(a) (an authorisation may limit the designated person's functions
-- to those specified) and s. 9B(3) (the CEO is to issue each designated
-- person a certificate) describe the authorisation's optional scope and its
-- evidentiary paper trail; neither is independently tested by any rule in
-- this Part. The certificate's existence is taken as a fact input to the
-- s. 9B(4) duty below rather than separately modelled.

DECLARE `S9B4 Facts` HAS
    `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom the designated person exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise a power under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate issued under s 9B(3) is produced in response`                                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9B(4)
GIVEN f IS A `S9B4 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the designated person complies with the s 9B(4) duty to produce the certificate` f MEANS
        (NOT f's `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom the designated person exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise a power under this Act`)
    OR  f's `certificate issued under s 9B(3) is produced in response`

§§ `10. Dogs not kept in district`

-- s. 10(1): deleted -- no content in the current compilation.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 10(2)
GIVEN `the place where the dog is ordinarily kept is not within the boundary of a district or of an area to which a s 9(1) Order applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog is deemed to be ordinarily kept within the nearest district under s 10(2)` `the place where the dog is ordinarily kept is not within the boundary of a district or of an area to which a s 9(1) Order applies` MEANS
    `the place where the dog is ordinarily kept is not within the boundary of a district or of an area to which a s 9(1) Order applies`

§§ `10AA. Delegation of local government powers and duties`

DECLARE `S10AA Delegation` HAS
    `made by absolute majority of the local government`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `expressly authorises the delegate to further delegate the power or duty` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 10AA(1)-(2)
GIVEN d IS A `S10AA Delegation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 10AA(1) delegation is validly made` d MEANS
    d's `made by absolute majority of the local government` AND d's `in writing`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 10AA(3)
GIVEN d IS A `S10AA Delegation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a further delegation by the s 10AA(1) delegate is authorised under s 10AA(3)` d MEANS
    `a s 10AA(1) delegation is validly made` d AND d's `expressly authorises the delegate to further delegate the power or duty`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 10AA(4)
GIVEN `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government's CEO is presumed to have acted within the terms of the s 10AA delegation` `the contrary is shown` MEANS
    NOT `the contrary is shown`

-- s. 10AA(5): the section does not limit the CEO's ability to perform a
-- function through an officer or agent (the local-government mirror of
-- s. 9A(5)). No fact this Part's rules would test; recorded as inert prose.

§§ `10AB. Register of, and review of, delegations`

-- s. 10AB(1): the duty to keep a register of s. 10AA(1) delegations and
-- further delegations is purely administrative machinery (record-keeping),
-- with no fact this Part's rules would test. Recorded as inert prose.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 10AB(2)
GIVEN `years since the delegator last reviewed the s 10AA(1) delegations and further delegations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 10AB(2) annual review duty is being complied with` `years since the delegator last reviewed the s 10AA(1) delegations and further delegations` MEANS
    `years since the delegator last reviewed the s 10AA(1) delegations and further delegations` AT MOST 1

§§ `10A. Payments to veterinarians towards cost of sterilisation`

DECLARE `S10A Eligible Person` HAS
    `is the registered owner of the dog, whether or not the registration is in the district of the local government or in another district` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resides in the district of the local government`                                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the local government's opinion, would suffer hardship in paying the whole of the cost of sterilisation of the dog`                    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 10A(3)
GIVEN p IS A `S10A Eligible Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A` p MEANS
        p's `is the registered owner of the dog, whether or not the registration is in the district of the local government or in another district`
    AND p's `resides in the district of the local government`
    AND p's `in the local government's opinion, would suffer hardship in paying the whole of the cost of sterilisation of the dog`

DECLARE `S10A Payment Facts` HAS
    `dog owned by an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `local government has issued directions in writing to the veterinarian under s 10A(1)(b)`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the local government is satisfied that the veterinarian has complied with those directions`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 10A(1)-(2)
GIVEN f IS A `S10A Payment Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 10A(1)(a) payment to the veterinarian may be made` f MEANS
        f's `dog owned by an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A`
    AND (   (NOT f's `local government has issued directions in writing to the veterinarian under s 10A(1)(b)`)
         OR f's `the local government is satisfied that the veterinarian has complied with those directions`)

§§ `11. Staff and services`

-- s. 11(1)-(2): power to establish dog management facilities and to enter
-- inter-council cooperation agreements is discretionary administrative
-- machinery, with no fact this Part's rules would test. Recorded as inert
-- prose.

-- s. 11(3) also imposes a first limb -- the local government's duty to
-- furnish the authorised person with a certificate evidencing appointment
-- -- alongside the person's duty to produce it on request. As with the
-- s. 9B(3) certificate-issuance precedent above, that furnishing duty is
-- purely evidentiary paper trail with no fact this Part's rules would
-- independently test; the certificate's existence is taken as a fact input
-- to the production duty below (via `certificate produced in response`)
-- rather than separately modelled.

DECLARE `S11 Certificate Facts` HAS
    `person is authorised by a local government to exercise a power under this Act`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom he exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate produced in response`                                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 11(5) exemption applies -- person appointed under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)`                              IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Local Government Act 1995 s. 9.10(2) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `Public Health Act 2016 s 31 disapplies or modifies the s 11(3) duty in this instance`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Public Health Act 2016 s. 31 -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 11(3), (5)
GIVEN f IS A `S11 Certificate Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 11(3) certificate-production duty applies to the person` f MEANS
        f's `person is authorised by a local government to exercise a power under this Act`
    AND NOT f's `s 11(5) exemption applies -- person appointed under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 11(3)-(4)
GIVEN f IS A `S11 Certificate Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person complies with the s 11(3) duty` f MEANS
        (NOT `the s 11(3) certificate-production duty applies to the person` f)
    OR  f's `Public Health Act 2016 s 31 disapplies or modifies the s 11(3) duty in this instance`
    OR  (NOT f's `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom he exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise the power`)
    OR  f's `certificate produced in response`

§§ `11A. Authorised persons`

-- s. 11A: the local government's CEO must, under the Local Government Act
-- 1995 s. 9.10(2), appoint persons to be authorised persons for the purposes
-- of this Act. An ongoing administrative duty with no numeric deadline; the
-- role it creates ("authorised person") is read by s. 12A below as an actor
-- category, not tested there as a fact about compliance with this duty.
-- Recorded as inert prose.

§§ `12. Joint jurisdiction`

DECLARE `S12 Pursuit Facts` HAS
    `person authorised to seize the dog in the district where the pursuit commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `person pursues that dog into another district of the State`                     IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 12(1)
GIVEN f IS A `S12 Pursuit Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 12(1) seizure authorisation continues into the district pursued into` f MEANS
    f's `person authorised to seize the dog in the district where the pursuit commenced` AND f's `person pursues that dog into another district of the State`

DECLARE `S12 Cooperation Agreement` HAS
    `2 or more local governments have entered into an agreement to cooperate in the administration of this Act`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement provides that an authorisation given by one has effect in the registration area administered by another` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 12(2)
GIVEN a IS A `S12 Cooperation Agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an authorisation given by one cooperating local government has effect in another's registration area under s 12(2)` a MEANS
    a's `2 or more local governments have entered into an agreement to cooperate in the administration of this Act` AND a's `the agreement provides that an authorisation given by one has effect in the registration area administered by another`

§§ `12A. Entry of premises`

DECLARE `S12A1 Entry Facts` HAS
    `occupier consents to entry`                                                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `premises is where a dog is registered to be, or (in an application for registration) described as, ordinarily kept`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose is to ascertain whether the dog is, or will be, effectively confined`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a dog is reasonably suspected to be in or at the premises`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose is to ascertain whether that suspected dog is registered for the purposes of s 7(1)`                               IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 7(1) -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 12A(1)
GIVEN f IS A `S12A1 Entry Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`entry and inspection under s 12A(1) is authorised` f MEANS
    LET `entry serves a permitted s 12A(1) purpose` MEANS
            (f's `premises is where a dog is registered to be, or (in an application for registration) described as, ordinarily kept`
             AND f's `purpose is to ascertain whether the dog is, or will be, effectively confined`)
        OR  (f's `a dog is reasonably suspected to be in or at the premises`
             AND f's `purpose is to ascertain whether that suspected dog is registered for the purposes of s 7(1)`)
    IN
        f's `occupier consents to entry` AND `entry serves a permitted s 12A(1) purpose`

DECLARE `S12A2 Entrant` IS ONE OF
    `Authorised Person`
    `Designated Person`
    `Person Named In The Warrant`

DECLARE `S12A2 Entry Facts` HAS
    `entry is under the authority of a warrant`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry is with the consent of an occupier who has reached 18 years of age`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act`                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- s. 12A(2A) ("without limiting subsection (2)") clarifies that determining
-- whether grounds exist for the cancellation of an approval to breed, a pet
-- shop approval or a dog supply approval is a purpose relating to the
-- enforcement of this Act. It is an interpretive gloss on `purpose relates
-- to the enforcement of this Act` above, not a fresh gate; the approval
-- machinery it names lies outside this chunk's assigned sections, so it is
-- recorded here as inert prose rather than a separate rule.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 12A(2)-(2A)
GIVEN entrant IS A `S12A2 Entrant`, f IS A `S12A2 Entry Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`entry and inspection under s 12A(2) is authorised` entrant f MEANS
    LET `entry is authorised by warrant or consent` MEANS
        CONSIDER entrant
        WHEN `Person Named In The Warrant` THEN f's `entry is under the authority of a warrant`
        OTHERWISE f's `entry is under the authority of a warrant` OR f's `entry is with the consent of an occupier who has reached 18 years of age`
    IN
        `entry is authorised by warrant or consent` AND f's `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 12A(3)
GIVEN `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied there are reasonable grounds for issuing a s 12A(2) warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Justice of the Peace may issue a s 12A(2) warrant` `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied there are reasonable grounds for issuing a s 12A(2) warrant` MEANS
    `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied there are reasonable grounds for issuing a s 12A(2) warrant`

DECLARE `S12A4 Entry Facts` HAS
    `premises is not a dwelling`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dangerous dog to be at the premises`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry at a reasonable time`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose is to ascertain whether an offence against Part VI Division 2 is being committed` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) Part VI Division 2 offences -- already encoded in dog-act-1976.l4, scoped out, fact-supplied (not imported here per the workflow's parallel-chunk rule)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 12A(4)
GIVEN f IS A `S12A4 Entry Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`entry under s 12A(4), without a warrant and without consent, is authorised` f MEANS
        f's `premises is not a dwelling`
    AND f's `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dangerous dog to be at the premises`
    AND f's `entry at a reasonable time`
    AND f's `purpose is to ascertain whether an offence against Part VI Division 2 is being committed`

DECLARE `S12A5 Vehicle Search Facts` HAS
    `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dog to be in the vehicle`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act`                      IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 12A(5)
GIVEN f IS A `S12A5 Vehicle Search Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`stopping, entering and searching or inspecting the vehicle under s 12A(5), without a warrant and without consent, is authorised` f MEANS
    f's `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dog to be in the vehicle` AND f's `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act`

§§ `13. Immunity of persons acting in good faith`

DECLARE `S13 Immunity Facts` HAS
    `act, matter or thing done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, in the exercise or purported exercise of a power or the performance of a duty under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, maliciously`                                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, without reasonable and probable cause`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 13
GIVEN f IS A `S13 Immunity Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13 immunity from proceedings applies` f MEANS
        f's `act, matter or thing done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, in the exercise or purported exercise of a power or the performance of a duty under this Act`
    AND NOT (   f's `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, maliciously`
             OR f's `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, without reasonable and probable cause`)

§§ `13A. Centralised registration system`

-- s. 13A(1): the CEO must establish and maintain the centralised
-- registration system -- purely administrative (infrastructure-building)
-- machinery, with no fact this Part's rules would test. Recorded as inert
-- prose.

DECLARE `S13A2 Compliance Facts` HAS
    `prescribed information recorded in the centralised registration system`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `information recorded is accurate and kept up to date`                    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 13A(2)
GIVEN f IS A `S13A2 Compliance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the CEO or local government complies with the s 13A(2) record-keeping duty` f MEANS
    f's `prescribed information recorded in the centralised registration system` AND f's `information recorded is accurate and kept up to date`

-- s. 13A(3)-(6): the power to correct errors, the permission to use the
-- system wherever this Act requires or permits something to be done "in a
-- manner approved by the CEO or a local government", the s. 54
-- regulation-making power over the system, and the CEO's power to combine
-- this database with the one kept under the Cat Act 2011 s. 41A(1), are all
-- discretionary administrative machinery with no fact this Part's rules
-- would test. Recorded as inert prose.

§§ `13B. Dog owner numbers`

DECLARE `S13B Person` HAS
    `owns, or has previously owned, 1 or more dogs`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `is of a class prescribed for the purposes of s 13B(1)(b)`         IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54 regulations -- scoped out, fact-supplied (no s 13B(1)(b) class has been prescribed within this chunk's source text)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 13B(1)
GIVEN p IS A `S13B Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is within the class of persons to whom a dog owner number may be issued under s 13B(1)` p MEANS
    p's `owns, or has previously owned, 1 or more dogs` OR p's `is of a class prescribed for the purposes of s 13B(1)(b)`

-- s. 13B(2): the s. 54 regulation-making power over dog owner numbers,
-- including a power to require one before a dog's ownership is transferred,
-- is an enabling provision over matters not yet prescribed; the dog-transfer
-- provisions it would interact with (ss 33GC, 33GE) lie in Part VI Division
-- 2, encoded separately in dog-act-1976.l4 and out of this chunk's range.
-- Recorded as inert prose.

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

-- s 9(1)
#ASSERT `the area is treated as within the local government's district under s 9(1)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the area is treated as within the local government's district under s 9(1)` FALSE)

-- s 9A
`a valid s 9A delegation` MEANS `S9A Delegation` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed by the CEO` IS TRUE
`an invalid s 9A delegation -- not signed by the CEO` MEANS `S9A Delegation` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed by the CEO` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a s 9A delegation is validly made` `a valid s 9A delegation`
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 9A delegation is validly made` `an invalid s 9A delegation -- not signed by the CEO`)

#ASSERT NOT `a s 9A delegate may validly sub-delegate the power or duty`

#ASSERT `the CEO's delegate is presumed to have acted within the terms of the s 9A delegation` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the CEO's delegate is presumed to have acted within the terms of the s 9A delegation` TRUE)

-- s 9B
`a s 9B(1) authorisation, in writing, not cancelled` MEANS `S9B Authorisation` WITH `made in writing by the CEO` IS TRUE, `cancelled by the CEO` IS FALSE
`a purported s 9B(1) authorisation, not in writing` MEANS `S9B Authorisation` WITH `made in writing by the CEO` IS FALSE, `cancelled by the CEO` IS FALSE
`a s 9B(1) authorisation later cancelled` MEANS `S9B Authorisation` WITH `made in writing by the CEO` IS TRUE, `cancelled by the CEO` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `a s 9B(1) authorisation is validly made` `a s 9B(1) authorisation, in writing, not cancelled`
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 9B(1) authorisation is validly made` `a purported s 9B(1) authorisation, not in writing`)
#ASSERT `a s 9B authorisation remains in force` `a s 9B(1) authorisation, in writing, not cancelled`
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 9B authorisation remains in force` `a s 9B(1) authorisation later cancelled`)

`s 9B(4) facts -- requested and produced` MEANS `S9B4 Facts` WITH `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom the designated person exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise a power under this Act` IS TRUE, `certificate issued under s 9B(3) is produced in response` IS TRUE
`s 9B(4) facts -- requested and withheld` MEANS `S9B4 Facts` WITH `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom the designated person exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise a power under this Act` IS TRUE, `certificate issued under s 9B(3) is produced in response` IS FALSE
`s 9B(4) facts -- no request made` MEANS `S9B4 Facts` WITH `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom the designated person exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise a power under this Act` IS FALSE, `certificate issued under s 9B(3) is produced in response` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the designated person complies with the s 9B(4) duty to produce the certificate` `s 9B(4) facts -- requested and produced`
#ASSERT NOT (`the designated person complies with the s 9B(4) duty to produce the certificate` `s 9B(4) facts -- requested and withheld`)
#ASSERT `the designated person complies with the s 9B(4) duty to produce the certificate` `s 9B(4) facts -- no request made`

-- s 10
#ASSERT `the dog is deemed to be ordinarily kept within the nearest district under s 10(2)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is deemed to be ordinarily kept within the nearest district under s 10(2)` FALSE)

-- s 10AA
`a valid s 10AA(1) delegation, sub-delegation authorised` MEANS `S10AA Delegation` WITH `made by absolute majority of the local government` IS TRUE, `in writing` IS TRUE, `expressly authorises the delegate to further delegate the power or duty` IS TRUE
`a valid s 10AA(1) delegation, sub-delegation not authorised` MEANS `S10AA Delegation` WITH `made by absolute majority of the local government` IS TRUE, `in writing` IS TRUE, `expressly authorises the delegate to further delegate the power or duty` IS FALSE
`an invalid s 10AA(1) delegation -- no absolute majority` MEANS `S10AA Delegation` WITH `made by absolute majority of the local government` IS FALSE, `in writing` IS TRUE, `expressly authorises the delegate to further delegate the power or duty` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `a s 10AA(1) delegation is validly made` `a valid s 10AA(1) delegation, sub-delegation authorised`
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 10AA(1) delegation is validly made` `an invalid s 10AA(1) delegation -- no absolute majority`)
#ASSERT `a further delegation by the s 10AA(1) delegate is authorised under s 10AA(3)` `a valid s 10AA(1) delegation, sub-delegation authorised`
#ASSERT NOT (`a further delegation by the s 10AA(1) delegate is authorised under s 10AA(3)` `a valid s 10AA(1) delegation, sub-delegation not authorised`)

#ASSERT `the local government's CEO is presumed to have acted within the terms of the s 10AA delegation` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the local government's CEO is presumed to have acted within the terms of the s 10AA delegation` TRUE)

-- s 10AB
#ASSERT `the s 10AB(2) annual review duty is being complied with` 0
#ASSERT `the s 10AB(2) annual review duty is being complied with` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 10AB(2) annual review duty is being complied with` 2)

-- s 10A
`an eligible person for a s 10A payment` MEANS `S10A Eligible Person` WITH `is the registered owner of the dog, whether or not the registration is in the district of the local government or in another district` IS TRUE, `resides in the district of the local government` IS TRUE, `in the local government's opinion, would suffer hardship in paying the whole of the cost of sterilisation of the dog` IS TRUE
`a non-resident registered owner, not eligible` MEANS `S10A Eligible Person` WITH `is the registered owner of the dog, whether or not the registration is in the district of the local government or in another district` IS TRUE, `resides in the district of the local government` IS FALSE, `in the local government's opinion, would suffer hardship in paying the whole of the cost of sterilisation of the dog` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the person is an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A` `an eligible person for a s 10A payment`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A` `a non-resident registered owner, not eligible`)

`s 10A payment facts -- no direction issued` MEANS `S10A Payment Facts` WITH `dog owned by an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A` IS TRUE, `local government has issued directions in writing to the veterinarian under s 10A(1)(b)` IS FALSE, `the local government is satisfied that the veterinarian has complied with those directions` IS FALSE
`s 10A payment facts -- direction issued and complied with` MEANS `S10A Payment Facts` WITH `dog owned by an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A` IS TRUE, `local government has issued directions in writing to the veterinarian under s 10A(1)(b)` IS TRUE, `the local government is satisfied that the veterinarian has complied with those directions` IS TRUE
`s 10A payment facts -- direction issued and not complied with` MEANS `S10A Payment Facts` WITH `dog owned by an eligible person for the purposes of s 10A` IS TRUE, `local government has issued directions in writing to the veterinarian under s 10A(1)(b)` IS TRUE, `the local government is satisfied that the veterinarian has complied with those directions` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a s 10A(1)(a) payment to the veterinarian may be made` `s 10A payment facts -- no direction issued`
#ASSERT `a s 10A(1)(a) payment to the veterinarian may be made` `s 10A payment facts -- direction issued and complied with`
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 10A(1)(a) payment to the veterinarian may be made` `s 10A payment facts -- direction issued and not complied with`)

-- s 11
`s 11(3) facts -- authorised, requested, produced` MEANS `S11 Certificate Facts` WITH `person is authorised by a local government to exercise a power under this Act` IS TRUE, `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom he exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise the power` IS TRUE, `certificate produced in response` IS TRUE, `s 11(5) exemption applies -- person appointed under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)` IS FALSE, `Public Health Act 2016 s 31 disapplies or modifies the s 11(3) duty in this instance` IS FALSE
`s 11(3) facts -- authorised, requested, withheld` MEANS `S11 Certificate Facts` WITH `person is authorised by a local government to exercise a power under this Act` IS TRUE, `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom he exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise the power` IS TRUE, `certificate produced in response` IS FALSE, `s 11(5) exemption applies -- person appointed under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)` IS FALSE, `Public Health Act 2016 s 31 disapplies or modifies the s 11(3) duty in this instance` IS FALSE
`s 11(3) facts -- s 11(5) exempt person, requested, withheld` MEANS `S11 Certificate Facts` WITH `person is authorised by a local government to exercise a power under this Act` IS TRUE, `reasonable request made by a person in respect of whom he exercises, has exercised, or is about to exercise the power` IS TRUE, `certificate produced in response` IS FALSE, `s 11(5) exemption applies -- person appointed under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)` IS TRUE, `Public Health Act 2016 s 31 disapplies or modifies the s 11(3) duty in this instance` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the s 11(3) certificate-production duty applies to the person` `s 11(3) facts -- authorised, requested, produced`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 11(3) certificate-production duty applies to the person` `s 11(3) facts -- s 11(5) exempt person, requested, withheld`)
#ASSERT `the person complies with the s 11(3) duty` `s 11(3) facts -- authorised, requested, produced`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person complies with the s 11(3) duty` `s 11(3) facts -- authorised, requested, withheld`)
#ASSERT `the person complies with the s 11(3) duty` `s 11(3) facts -- s 11(5) exempt person, requested, withheld`

-- s 12
`s 12(1) pursuit into another district` MEANS `S12 Pursuit Facts` WITH `person authorised to seize the dog in the district where the pursuit commenced` IS TRUE, `person pursues that dog into another district of the State` IS TRUE
`s 12(1) unauthorised person, pursuit` MEANS `S12 Pursuit Facts` WITH `person authorised to seize the dog in the district where the pursuit commenced` IS FALSE, `person pursues that dog into another district of the State` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the s 12(1) seizure authorisation continues into the district pursued into` `s 12(1) pursuit into another district`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 12(1) seizure authorisation continues into the district pursued into` `s 12(1) unauthorised person, pursuit`)

`s 12(2) cooperation agreement, reciprocal effect` MEANS `S12 Cooperation Agreement` WITH `2 or more local governments have entered into an agreement to cooperate in the administration of this Act` IS TRUE, `the agreement provides that an authorisation given by one has effect in the registration area administered by another` IS TRUE
`s 12(2) agreement without reciprocal-effect term` MEANS `S12 Cooperation Agreement` WITH `2 or more local governments have entered into an agreement to cooperate in the administration of this Act` IS TRUE, `the agreement provides that an authorisation given by one has effect in the registration area administered by another` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `an authorisation given by one cooperating local government has effect in another's registration area under s 12(2)` `s 12(2) cooperation agreement, reciprocal effect`
#ASSERT NOT (`an authorisation given by one cooperating local government has effect in another's registration area under s 12(2)` `s 12(2) agreement without reciprocal-effect term`)

-- s 12A
`s 12A(1)(a) entry, confinement check, consented` MEANS `S12A1 Entry Facts` WITH `occupier consents to entry` IS TRUE, `premises is where a dog is registered to be, or (in an application for registration) described as, ordinarily kept` IS TRUE, `purpose is to ascertain whether the dog is, or will be, effectively confined` IS TRUE, `a dog is reasonably suspected to be in or at the premises` IS FALSE, `purpose is to ascertain whether that suspected dog is registered for the purposes of s 7(1)` IS FALSE
`s 12A(1)(b) entry, registration check, consented` MEANS `S12A1 Entry Facts` WITH `occupier consents to entry` IS TRUE, `premises is where a dog is registered to be, or (in an application for registration) described as, ordinarily kept` IS FALSE, `purpose is to ascertain whether the dog is, or will be, effectively confined` IS FALSE, `a dog is reasonably suspected to be in or at the premises` IS TRUE, `purpose is to ascertain whether that suspected dog is registered for the purposes of s 7(1)` IS TRUE
`s 12A(1) entry, no occupier consent` MEANS `S12A1 Entry Facts` WITH `occupier consents to entry` IS FALSE, `premises is where a dog is registered to be, or (in an application for registration) described as, ordinarily kept` IS TRUE, `purpose is to ascertain whether the dog is, or will be, effectively confined` IS TRUE, `a dog is reasonably suspected to be in or at the premises` IS FALSE, `purpose is to ascertain whether that suspected dog is registered for the purposes of s 7(1)` IS FALSE
`s 12A(1) entry, consented but neither (a) nor (b) purpose made out` MEANS `S12A1 Entry Facts` WITH `occupier consents to entry` IS TRUE, `premises is where a dog is registered to be, or (in an application for registration) described as, ordinarily kept` IS FALSE, `purpose is to ascertain whether the dog is, or will be, effectively confined` IS FALSE, `a dog is reasonably suspected to be in or at the premises` IS FALSE, `purpose is to ascertain whether that suspected dog is registered for the purposes of s 7(1)` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `entry and inspection under s 12A(1) is authorised` `s 12A(1)(a) entry, confinement check, consented`
#ASSERT `entry and inspection under s 12A(1) is authorised` `s 12A(1)(b) entry, registration check, consented`
#ASSERT NOT (`entry and inspection under s 12A(1) is authorised` `s 12A(1) entry, no occupier consent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`entry and inspection under s 12A(1) is authorised` `s 12A(1) entry, consented but neither (a) nor (b) purpose made out`)

`s 12A(2) facts -- warrant, enforcement purpose` MEANS `S12A2 Entry Facts` WITH `entry is under the authority of a warrant` IS TRUE, `entry is with the consent of an occupier who has reached 18 years of age` IS FALSE, `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act` IS TRUE
`s 12A(2) facts -- adult occupier consent, enforcement purpose` MEANS `S12A2 Entry Facts` WITH `entry is under the authority of a warrant` IS FALSE, `entry is with the consent of an occupier who has reached 18 years of age` IS TRUE, `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act` IS TRUE
`s 12A(2) facts -- neither warrant nor adult consent` MEANS `S12A2 Entry Facts` WITH `entry is under the authority of a warrant` IS FALSE, `entry is with the consent of an occupier who has reached 18 years of age` IS FALSE, `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `entry and inspection under s 12A(2) is authorised` `Authorised Person` `s 12A(2) facts -- warrant, enforcement purpose`
#ASSERT `entry and inspection under s 12A(2) is authorised` `Designated Person` `s 12A(2) facts -- adult occupier consent, enforcement purpose`
#ASSERT `entry and inspection under s 12A(2) is authorised` `Person Named In The Warrant` `s 12A(2) facts -- warrant, enforcement purpose`
#ASSERT NOT (`entry and inspection under s 12A(2) is authorised` `Person Named In The Warrant` `s 12A(2) facts -- adult occupier consent, enforcement purpose`)
#ASSERT NOT (`entry and inspection under s 12A(2) is authorised` `Authorised Person` `s 12A(2) facts -- neither warrant nor adult consent`)

#ASSERT `a Justice of the Peace may issue a s 12A(2) warrant` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a Justice of the Peace may issue a s 12A(2) warrant` FALSE)

`s 12A(4) facts -- non-dwelling, suspected dangerous dog` MEANS `S12A4 Entry Facts` WITH `premises is not a dwelling` IS TRUE, `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dangerous dog to be at the premises` IS TRUE, `entry at a reasonable time` IS TRUE, `purpose is to ascertain whether an offence against Part VI Division 2 is being committed` IS TRUE
`s 12A(4) facts -- premises is a dwelling` MEANS `S12A4 Entry Facts` WITH `premises is not a dwelling` IS FALSE, `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dangerous dog to be at the premises` IS TRUE, `entry at a reasonable time` IS TRUE, `purpose is to ascertain whether an offence against Part VI Division 2 is being committed` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `entry under s 12A(4), without a warrant and without consent, is authorised` `s 12A(4) facts -- non-dwelling, suspected dangerous dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`entry under s 12A(4), without a warrant and without consent, is authorised` `s 12A(4) facts -- premises is a dwelling`)

`s 12A(5) facts -- suspected dog in vehicle, enforcement purpose` MEANS `S12A5 Vehicle Search Facts` WITH `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dog to be in the vehicle` IS TRUE, `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act` IS TRUE
`s 12A(5) facts -- no suspicion` MEANS `S12A5 Vehicle Search Facts` WITH `an authorised person reasonably suspects a dog to be in the vehicle` IS FALSE, `purpose relates to the enforcement of this Act` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `stopping, entering and searching or inspecting the vehicle under s 12A(5), without a warrant and without consent, is authorised` `s 12A(5) facts -- suspected dog in vehicle, enforcement purpose`
#ASSERT NOT (`stopping, entering and searching or inspecting the vehicle under s 12A(5), without a warrant and without consent, is authorised` `s 12A(5) facts -- no suspicion`)

-- s 13
`s 13 facts -- good faith exercise of power, no malice, reasonable cause` MEANS `S13 Immunity Facts` WITH `act, matter or thing done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, in the exercise or purported exercise of a power or the performance of a duty under this Act` IS TRUE, `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, maliciously` IS FALSE, `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, without reasonable and probable cause` IS FALSE
`s 13 facts -- malicious exercise of power` MEANS `S13 Immunity Facts` WITH `act, matter or thing done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, in the exercise or purported exercise of a power or the performance of a duty under this Act` IS TRUE, `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, maliciously` IS TRUE, `done, commanded to be done, or omitted to be done, without reasonable and probable cause` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 13 immunity from proceedings applies` `s 13 facts -- good faith exercise of power, no malice, reasonable cause`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 13 immunity from proceedings applies` `s 13 facts -- malicious exercise of power`)

